- Generator. On close (GeneratorExit), close resource exactly once.
- Constructing or closing unstarted generator: no read, no close. That's naturally handled since code after first yield doesn't run if unstarted; generator.close() on unstarted generator just closes it without entering body. Wait — generator.close() on a not-yet-started generator throws GeneratorExit at the start... Actually closing an unstarted generator does run GeneratorExit at the first line? No: closing an unstarted generator raises GeneratorExit inside at the beginning of the body — Python: if the generator hasn't started, close() just marks it closed without executing body code. Yes, per CPython: "If the generator is not yet started, close() will just close it" — the body never runs. So lazy try/finally works.

- On exhaustion and on errors: close resource exactly once.
